ity  of the issues  we ignored the signals about the need  for additional time to refine  the game on base last gen consoles it  was the wrong approach and against our  business philosophy  on top of that during the campaign we  showed the game mostly on pcs  end quote from there the lawsuit alleges  that by  making these false or misleading  statements cdpr  violated various sections of the  exchange act  and the exchange act basically  encompasses all of the rules laws and  regulations around buying and selling  stocks in the united states  quote because of their positions of  control and authority as senior officers  the individual defendants were able to  and did  control the contents of the various  reports press releases and public  filings which the company disseminated  in the marketplace  during the class period throughout the  class period the individual defendants  exercised their power and authority  to cause the company to engage in the  wrongful acts complained of herein  end quote what the lawsuit is saying  here is that senior management at cdpr  had control and final say over messaging  and marketing around the game  and either lied misrepresented or  straight up just  didn't tell anybody that the game was  busted and remember because cdpr  management allegedly lied about the  state of the game investors lost  1.8 billion dollars you'd expect people  to be  pretty heated and then finally the  lawsuits ask that cdpr pay for damages  and  court fees and then demand a jury trial  and while both  these lawsuits read as too gigantic this  you  twitter threads it'll be interesting to  see what impact  if any these court cases have on the  games industry as a whole  and as if that wasn't enough cdpr are  breaking their game in new ways  while trying to fix it they recently  announced  two gigantic patches they hoped would  fix everything  but instead it just introduced a new  game-breaking bug  essentially what's happening is that  dialogue that's supposed to trigger  and move a quest forward doesn't happen  and then you're stuck this was enough of  a reoccurring problem that on january  23rd  cdpr put out a statement basically  saying hey here's a workaround  just load in a different safe which is  truly what you don't want to see  so really it turns out that cyberpunk  2077 is not the boundary pushing  revolutionary video game people wanted  or thought it was going to be  it's a pretty ordinary even fun game  with a ton of ordinary and industry  specific  problems that have been around for  decades at this point  and honestly that's all it was ever  going to be  i'm trying man all right  i'm trying  i can't we're in the middle of a  lockdown  i know i know there is and the funny  thing about all this  i look like an insane person because  nobody can hear what you're saying to me  i'm not like i'm not grumpy at any at  you or in any person  well we have our m board  that hurt my hand
 

